==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|finaunce}}, {{m|enm|fynaunce}}, from {{der|en|xno|-}}, {{der|en|frm|finance}}, from {{m|frm|finer||to pay ransom}} (whence also {{cog|en|fine||to pay a penalty}}), from {{m|frm|fin||end}}, from {{der|en|la|fīnis}}.<ref name="oetyld">{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref><ref>{{R:American Heritage 2000}}</ref>
Original English sense that appeared c. 1400 was “ending”. The sense of “ending or satisfying a debt” originated from French influence: in the sense of “ransom” appeared in the mid 15th century, in the sense of “taxation” appeared in the late 15th century. In the sense of “manage money” first recorded c. 1770.<ref name="oetyld" />

